00:47:55,874 --> 00:47:58,209
<i>but the hours were long
and the money was horseshit.</i>

784
00:48:01,046 --> 00:48:04,841
<i>So I bought a typewriter
and set myself up as a public stenographer.</i>

785
00:48:06,885 --> 00:48:07,886
<i>What a laugh.</i>

786
00:48:09,763 --> 00:48:12,807
<i>In four months I typed six letters
and one manuscript.</i>

787
00:48:13,558 --> 00:48:17,062
<i>The manuscript was for</i> Real Life Tales
<i>and a total waste of paper.</i>

788
00:48:17,145 --> 00:48:18,897
<i>But the jerk who wrote it, sold it.</i>

789
00:48:19,064 --> 00:48:20,190
<i>Which gave me an idea.</i>

790
00:48:23,943 --> 00:48:26,946
<i>I bought a stack of confession magazines
and studied them.</i>

791
00:48:35,830 --> 00:48:37,082
<i>The words came easy.</i>

792
00:48:39,000 --> 00:48:41,169
<i>The Unmarried Mother was born.</i>

793
00:48:43,880 --> 00:48:46,257
<i>So, now you know how I get
the authentic woman's angle</i>

794
00:48:46,841 --> 00:48:48,635
on an Unmarried Mother story.

795
00:48:49,177 --> 00:48:51,346
Through the only version I haven't sold.

796
00:48:52,055 --> 00:48:53,056
The true one.

797
00:48:54,808 --> 00:48:57,185
So, do I win the bottle?

798
00:49:00,230 --> 00:49:01,231
Not bad.

799
00:49:03,108 --> 00:49:04,192
Not bad.

800
00:49:07,028 --> 00:49:08,947
So, is that it? Story's over?

801
00:49:09,322 --> 00:49:11,116
Yeah, afraid so.

802
00:49:12,283 --> 00:49:15,161
The man that ruined my life is a ghost
and so is my daughter.

803
00:49:15,787 --> 00:49:17,956
I guess at some point you just
gotta let things go.

804
00:49:18,039 --> 00:49:19,040
And have you?

805
00:49:19,332 --> 00:49:20,333
Fuck no.

806
00:49:24,587 --> 00:49:26,256
What if I could put him in front of you?

807
00:49:27,715 --> 00:49:29,217
The man that ruined your life.

808
00:49:30,176 --> 00:49:32,303
And if I could guarantee you

809
00:49:32,637 --> 00:49:33,888
that you'd get away with it.

810
00:49:36,182 --> 00:49:37,225
Would you kill him?

811
00:49:39,811 --> 00:49:40,854
In a heartbeat.

812
00:49:42,981 --> 00:49:44,023
I know where he is.

813
00:49:45,775 --> 00:49:46,943
Yeah, of course you do.

814
00:49:47,026 --> 00:49:48,027
No bullshit.

815
00:49:48,361 --> 00:49:50,029
And how the hell do you know that?

816
00:49:53,366 --> 00:49:54,367
There are records.

817
00:49:54,868 --> 00:49:57,871
Hospital records, orphanage records,
medical records...

818
00:49:57,954 --> 00:49:58,997
Been there, done that.

819
00:49:59,998 --> 00:50:01,291
Beth Fetherage.

820
00:50:02,250 --> 00:50:04,419
Wasn't that the name of your caretaker
at the orphanage?

821
00:50:04,919 --> 00:50:05,920
Beth?

822
00:50:07,672 --> 00:50:08,756
You son of a bitch.

823
00:50:08,923 --> 00:50:10,008
Have you been following me?

824
00:50:10,091 --> 00:50:11,593
Son of a bitch. That's funny.

825
00:50:12,594 --> 00:50:13,595
No.

826
00:50:13,678 --> 00:50:16,264
Your name, as a woman, was Jane, right?

827
00:50:16,389 --> 00:50:18,725
You told me that. You didn't tell me
your name as a man.

828
00:50:18,808 --> 00:50:21,728
John. Which is not terribly original,
by the way.

829
00:50:21,853 --> 00:50:23,021
What are you, a cop or something?

830
00:50:23,229 --> 00:50:25,190
I can put this guy in your lap.

831
00:50:26,441 --> 00:50:28,193
You can do whatever you want

832
00:50:28,860 --> 00:50:31,946
and I guarantee you you'll get away with it.

833
00:50:37,035 --> 00:50:38,203
All right, where is he?

834
00:50:41,789 --> 00:50:43,166
I do something for you

835
00:50:43,833 --> 00:50:45,126
and you do something for me.

836
00:50:46,211 --> 00:50:47,295
Fuck you.

837
00:50:47,921 --> 00:50:49,297
Okay, well,

838
00:50:50,048 --> 00:50:51,132
enjoy your prize.

839
00:50:53,134 --> 00:50:54,135
What do I have to do?

840
00:50:54,344 --> 00:50:55,345
You like your job?

841
00:50:55,637 --> 00:50:56,679
Hell, no.

842
00:50:56,763 --> 00:50:58,139
Nobody's ever given you a break, right?

843
00:50:58,848 --> 00:51:00,225
Did you listen to my story?

844
00:51:00,475 --> 00:51:02,894
Yeah, and you excelled during your
service training.

845
00:51:02,977 --> 00:51:03,937
Excelled.

846
00:51:04,020 --> 00:51:06,272
You have skills you've never had
the chance to use

847
00:51:06,356 --> 00:51:07,732
and I can give you that chance.

848
00:51:08,441 --> 00:51:09,442
Let me put it this way.

849
00:51:10,109 --> 00:51:11,861
I hand him to you, you do whatever you like.

850
00:51:12,320 --> 00:51:14,447
And when you're done, you try my job.

851
00:51:14,530 --> 00:51:15,698
You don't like it, you walk away.

852
00:51:18,243 --> 00:51:20,245
You're not talking about bartending are you?

853
00:51:21,162 --> 00:51:23,164
I'm not talking about bartending.

854
00:51:23,915 --> 00:51:24,916
What is it?

855
00:51:25,917 --> 00:51:26,918
I'll show you.

856
00:51:27,001 --> 00:51:28,002
No. Fuck that, no.

857
00:51:28,086 --> 00:51:30,046
Stop playing games. Just tell me right now.

858
00:51:30,129 --> 00:51:32,423
Look, Robertson explains it so much better
than I do.

859
00:51:34,842 --> 00:51:35,843
Don't mess with me.

860
00:51:36,386 --> 00:51:38,096
What, you're working with Robertson?

861
00:51:38,179 --> 00:51:40,098
Yes, I am, and he wants me to help you.

862
00:51:41,266 --> 00:51:43,226
You're part of Robertson's
little secret society?

863
00:51:43,309 --> 00:51:44,310
Yes.

864
00:51:44,811 --> 00:51:46,271
Tell me what it's all about then.

865
00:51:48,398 --> 00:51:49,732
First things first.

866
00:51:50,108 --> 00:51:52,527
Jerry! I'm going on a break.

867
00:51:59,200 --> 00:52:00,326
Oh, fuck.

868
00:52:09,043 --> 00:52:10,044
Where is he?

869
00:52:10,503 --> 00:52:11,504
What, is he down there?

870
00:52:12,130 --> 00:52:14,132
Listen, you're just going to have to trust me,
all right?

871
00:52:15,216 --> 00:52:16,342
Now I must be drunk.

872
00:52:17,510 --> 00:52:18,970
You better not be fucking with me.

873
00:52:20,221 --> 00:52:22,181
You think I might be the Fizzle Bomber?

874
00:52:22,557 --> 00:52:23,558
Maybe.

875
00:52:24,058 --> 00:52:25,435
What if you're the Fizzle Bomber?

876
00:52:25,893 --> 00:52:26,936
What if I am?

877
00:52:28,062 --> 00:52:29,147
Well, come on.

878
00:52:29,272 --> 00:52:30,440
This is what you wanted, right?

879
00:52:30,565 --> 00:52:31,566
Come on.

880
00:52:35,528 --> 00:52:38,489
<i>I'm my own grandpa</i>

881
00:52:38,573 --> 00:52:39,574
Here we go.

882
00:52:40,199 --> 00:52:41,284
All right.

883
00:52:42,994 --> 00:52:44,954
Follow me right in here.

884
00:52:46,789 --> 00:52:48,833
Can't be too cautious these days.

885
00:52:56,341 --> 00:52:57,342
What are you doing?

886
00:53:00,261 --> 00:53:01,971
Killing somebody's not easy, you know.

887
00:53:04,390 --> 00:53:08,102
No matter how much hate and anger
you may have in your heart,

888
00:53:08,394 --> 00:53:10,229
when it comes time to pull the trigger

889
00:53:10,355 --> 00:53:11,481
most people can't do it.

890
00:53:12,148 --> 00:53:13,399
You speaking from experience?

891
00:53:13,816 --> 00:53:15,443
I'm just telling you the truth.

892
00:53:18,863 --> 00:53:19,947
Well, I'm not afraid.

893
00:53:20,114 --> 00:53:22,116
You bring him to me and I won't hesitate.

894
00:53:22,950 --> 00:53:24,118
All right, that's good.

895
00:53:25,953 --> 00:53:27,038
So, where is he?

896
00:53:27,121 --> 00:53:28,122
Hold your horses.

897
00:53:33,044 --> 00:53:34,128
What, are you going to play for me?

898
00:53:34,379 --> 00:53:36,130
No, no. I'm going to play you the past.

899
00:53:37,215 --> 00:53:41,469
This is a USFF Coordinates
Transformer Field Kit.

900
00:53:42,053 --> 00:53:43,054
No moving parts.

901
00:53:43,137 --> 00:53:45,848
It weighs approximately six kilos,
fully charged.

902
00:53:46,140 --> 00:53:48,643
I've adjusted it to support our body mass.

903
00:53:48,976 --> 00:53:51,604
It will calculate a discreet arrival location

904
00:53:51,687 --> 00:53:54,941
and avoid any materialization collisions.

905
00:53:55,733 --> 00:53:56,734
So, what is it?

906
00:53:57,902 --> 00:54:00,655
It's a device that creates a temporal wake.

907
00:54:01,239 --> 00:54:02,240
A what?

908
00:54:02,907 --> 00:54:03,950
It's a time machine.

909
00:54:06,077 --> 00:54:07,286
You gotta be shitting me.

910
00:54:07,370 --> 00:54:10,331
No, I am not.

911
00:54:12,959 --> 00:54:14,335
Look, don't be alarmed, all right?

912
00:54:14,419 --> 00:54:15,503
You have to stand closer.

913
00:54:15,711 --> 00:54:17,213
You have to be within three feet.

914
00:54:17,630 --> 00:54:19,048
What have you got two guns for?

915
00:54:19,340 --> 00:54:20,341
Don't worry.

916
00:54:21,175 --> 00:54:22,176
I've done this a lot.

917
00:54:25,346 --> 00:54:27,432
Seriously, pal, you need to stop
playing games with me.

918
00:54:27,515 --> 00:54:29,976
Stand still, okay?

919
00:54:30,059 --> 00:54:31,436
Take a deep breath and hold this.

920
00:54:31,519 --> 00:54:34,397
Hold it.
It's okay. Here you go.

921
00:54:37,024 --> 00:54:38,484
Now, you just have to close your eyes.

922
00:54:39,444 --> 00:54:40,987
Why do I need to close my eyes...

923
00:54:48,202 --> 00:54:50,037
- God, what was that?
- Yeah.

924
00:54:50,121 --> 00:54:51,164
The time distortion field.

925
00:54:51,581 --> 00:54:53,207
- You're going to be fine.
- What?

926
00:54:53,458 --> 00:54:55,126
Just take some deep breaths, all right?

927
00:54:55,209 --> 00:54:56,210
What is this?

928
00:54:56,335 --> 00:54:57,587
Just take some deep breaths.

929
00:54:57,920 --> 00:54:59,714
The first few jumps can really
knock you around.

930
00:55:01,299 --> 00:55:02,842
- Jumps?
- Yeah.

931
00:55:03,217 --> 00:55:06,554
We're in Cleveland, Ohio, April 3rd, 1963.

932
00:55:09,348 --> 00:55:10,349
What?

933
00:55:10,516 --> 00:55:11,517
That's impossible.

934
00:55:11,934 --> 00:55:12,935
I know.

935
00:55:13,019 --> 00:55:15,855
Look, in this job you can't afford
to make any mistakes.

936
00:55:15,938 --> 00:55:17,690
Timing is essential.

937
00:55:19,358 --> 00:55:20,485
I've got some money for you.

938
00:55:20,735 --> 00:55:23,154
The Temporal Bureau doesn't care
how much money you spend.

939
00:55:23,237 --> 00:55:24,280
It doesn't matter to them.

940
00:55:24,363 --> 00:55:26,532
What they don't like is any
unnecessary anachronisms.

941
00:55:26,949 --> 00:55:27,992
The Temporal Bureau?

942
00:55:28,075 --> 00:55:29,452
Is that the company you work for?

943
00:55:29,577 --> 00:55:31,621
That's right. The one you almost worked for.

944
00:55:32,288 --> 00:55:33,331
So, where's Robertson?

945
00:55:33,748 --> 00:55:35,124
He's in 1985.

946
00:55:35,833 --> 00:55:36,834
What?

947
00:55:37,251 --> 00:55:38,377
At Bureau headquarters.

948
00:55:42,298 --> 00:55:44,008
So what, you're a cop?

949
00:55:44,759 --> 00:55:46,469
I'm a Temporal Agent, one of 11.

950
00:55:46,677 --> 00:55:48,721
We prevent crime before it takes place.

951
00:55:49,180 --> 00:55:51,390
Here. Here's some clothes.
Put them on.

952
00:55:53,351 --> 00:55:55,269
Well, how did you know
the clothes would be there?

953
00:55:55,436 --> 00:55:57,480
Doesn't matter. We just need
to start blending in.

954
00:55:58,147 --> 00:55:59,440
What, have you been here before?

955
00:56:00,358 --> 00:56:01,692
It's complicated, all right?

956
00:56:02,443 --> 00:56:03,444
Yeah, no shit.

957
00:56:03,569 --> 00:56:05,530
Look, our time disruption footprint

958
00:56:05,613 --> 00:56:07,490
needs to be extremely small.

959
00:56:07,615 --> 00:56:09,992
The Bureau allows for slight variations

960
00:56:10,076 --> 00:56:12,078
but ultimately the parameters
are extremely strict.

961
00:56:12,161 --> 00:56:14,497
Any deviation from our mission
results in termination.

962
00:56:14,705 --> 00:56:16,207
Termination of your job?

963
00:56:16,290 --> 00:56:17,583
Termination of your life.

964
00:56:18,084 --> 00:56:20,711
That's why you want to keep your
conversations to people in this time period

965
00:56:21,045 --> 00:56:22,421
to an absolute minimum.

966
00:56:23,130 --> 00:56:24,131
This time period.

967
00:56:25,174 --> 00:56:27,635
Okay. So how far can you travel, then?

968
00:56:28,135 --> 00:56:32,139
Travel beyond 53 years of zero point,
either direction,

969
00:56:32,557 --> 00:56:34,475
will result in the temporal wake
disintegrating.

970
00:56:34,684 --> 00:56:35,685
Zero point?

971
00:56:37,311 --> 00:56:38,604
The invention of time travel.

972
00:56:38,729 --> 00:56:39,730
And when's that?

973
00:56:40,064 --> 00:56:42,358
It will be in 1981.

974
00:56:44,485 --> 00:56:45,486
Right.

975
00:56:46,487 --> 00:56:47,488
I can't believe this.

976
00:56:47,989 --> 00:56:49,031
And so,

977
00:56:49,115 --> 00:56:52,118
I get to be one of these, you know,
a Temporal Agent?

978
00:56:52,702 --> 00:56:54,120
If you prove yourself.

979
00:56:55,746 --> 00:56:56,747
Right.

980
00:56:58,749 --> 00:57:00,167
So what's this guy to you?

981
00:57:00,418 --> 00:57:03,588
Well, I'm starting to suspect that he might
be the Fizzle Bomber. All right?

982
00:57:03,754 --> 00:57:06,674
But all that's clear is he's the main obstacle
that's held you back.

983
00:57:07,675 --> 00:57:09,510
So, I kill him

984
00:57:10,344 --> 00:57:11,554
you take me to Robertson

985
00:57:11,637 --> 00:57:12,763
and you show me everything.

986
00:57:13,139 --> 00:57:14,140
Agreed.

987
00:57:15,182 --> 00:57:16,684
Right. Okay, so where is he?

988
00:57:16,767 --> 00:57:18,144
Okay. Hey, hey.

989
00:57:18,853 --> 00:57:19,854
Are you all right?

990
00:57:20,605 --> 00:57:21,606
Yeah.

991
00:57:22,398 --> 00:57:25,234
All right, he's at Cleveland College,
five blocks from here.

992
00:57:25,359 --> 00:57:27,862
You remember? He's on his way
to meet Jane. You.

993
00:57:28,154 --> 00:57:29,697
The 1963 you.

994
00:57:29,864 --> 00:57:30,990
Yeah, I remember.

995
00:57:31,073 --> 00:57:32,074
Okay, great.

996
00:57:33,868 --> 00:57:37,830
So, I can do this?
I can change my past?

997
00:57:38,205 --> 00:57:39,206
Yes, you can.

998
00:57:40,416 --> 00:57:42,251
Have you ever thought about
changing yours?

999
00:57:43,669 --> 00:57:45,296
I never deviate from the mission.

1000
00:57:47,590 --> 00:57:49,342
- Never?
- Never.

1001
00:57:51,552 --> 00:57:53,512
Look, I'll pick you up
when you're done, all right?

1002
00:57:53,596 --> 00:57:55,139
No. Whoa, where are you going?

1003
00:57:55,264 --> 00:57:57,475
Don't worry. I'll be around, trust me.

1004
00:57:57,558 --> 00:57:58,559
Do I...

1005
00:58:00,311 --> 00:58:01,604
Do I have a choice?

1006
00:58:02,146 --> 00:58:03,898
Of course. You always have a choice.

1007
00:58:04,398 --> 00:58:06,901
Yeah, but sometimes don't you think
that things are just inevitable?

1008
00:58:09,236 --> 00:58:10,988
Yes, the thought has crossed my mind.

1009
00:58:14,116 --> 00:58:15,826
This life.

1010
00:58:16,744 --> 00:58:17,745
Is it lonely?

1011
00:58:21,957 --> 00:58:22,958
No family.

1012
00:58:24,585 --> 00:58:25,586
No.

1013
00:58:27,254 --> 00:58:29,632
But, you do have a purpose.

1014
00:58:33,886 --> 00:58:34,887
Right.

1015
00:59:25,146 --> 00:59:26,188
Oh, I'm so sorry.

1016
00:59:27,982 --> 00:59:29,024
Are you lost?

1017
00:59:30,317 --> 00:59:31,610
No, I'm looking for someone.

1018
00:59:32,069 --> 00:59:33,738
Thanks, I'll just wait.

1019
00:59:33,821 --> 00:59:36,866
Well, you know what they say about
good things happening to those who wait.

1020
00:59:43,497 --> 00:59:46,208
But only the things left behind
by those who hustle.

1021
00:59:53,632 --> 00:59:55,468
I was thinking the exact same thing.

1022
00:59:56,260 --> 00:59:57,261
What are the odds?

1023
01:00:00,139 --> 01:00:01,182
What are the odds.

1024
01:00:04,643 --> 01:00:05,644
Are you okay?

1025
01:00:07,730 --> 01:00:09,857
You're not how I imagined you'd look.

1026
01:00:11,984 --> 01:00:12,985
Do I know you?

1027
01:00:16,447 --> 01:00:17,531
You're beautiful.

1028
01:00:21,619 --> 01:00:23,245
Someone should have told you that.

1029
01:00:27,374 --> 01:00:28,542
Well, you just did.

1030
01:00:42,515 --> 01:00:44,892
<i>If you ever want to stop the Fizzle Bomber</i>

1031
01:00:45,810 --> 01:00:47,394
<i>you'll never get another chance.</i>

1032
01:04:39,793 --> 01:04:40,794
Come on, come on.

1033
01:05:27,883 --> 01:05:30,385
<i>Sometimes don't you think that things
are just inevitable?</i>

1034
01:05:32,471 --> 01:05:34,515
<i>Yes, the thought has crossed my mind.</i>

1035
01:05:47,694 --> 01:05:49,780
Time travel can be disorienting.

1036
01:05:50,572 --> 01:05:52,866
Even short jumps
can knock you around a bit.

1037
01:05:53,909 --> 01:05:55,869
Don't ever exceed the jump limit.

1038
01:05:57,121 --> 01:05:58,872
It can be problematic.

1039
01:06:01,166 --> 01:06:02,417
Deep breaths.

1040
01:06:03,210 --> 01:06:04,503
<i>They always help.</i>

1041
01:06:13,720 --> 01:06:15,722
I don't get out and meet a lot of new people.

1042
01:06:19,935 --> 01:06:20,936
Why not?

1043
01:06:23,647 --> 01:06:24,815
I don't know. I just don't.

1044
01:06:31,989 --> 01:06:33,073
Are you nervous?

1045
01:06:35,117 --> 01:06:36,118
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>

1046
01:06:36,451 --> 01:06:39,204
<i>Don't forget to buy a hat, gloves and a jacket.</i>

1047
01:06:39,454 --> 01:06:41,748
It's cold this time of year, back in '64.

1048
01:06:43,750 --> 01:06:46,044
This is a job, all right? Remember that.

1049
01:06:46,128 --> 01:06:49,214
It's unlike any other, but you still have
tasks to perform

1050
01:06:49,298 --> 01:06:50,424
deadlines to meet.

1051
01:06:50,716 --> 01:06:52,718
Some days those tasks are easier than others

1052
01:06:52,801 --> 01:06:55,179
but it's imperative that you succeed.

1053
01:06:59,683 --> 01:07:01,685
<i>You always knew this day would come.</i>

1054
01:07:06,773 --> 01:07:07,858
You can do this.

1055
01:07:09,860 --> 01:07:11,069
<i>Why don't you meet new people?</i>

1056
01:07:13,530 --> 01:07:15,490
I'm not very good in social situations.

1057
01:07:15,699 --> 01:07:17,159
Some people just don't like me, I guess.

1058
01:07:17,701 --> 01:07:18,785
Why is that, do you think?

1059
01:07:19,453 --> 01:07:20,454
I don't know.

1060
01:07:21,288 --> 01:07:22,956
Perhaps it's because you think
you're better than them.

1061
01:07:24,291 --> 01:07:25,292
Excuse me?

1062
01:07:26,960 --> 01:07:28,212
Well, you think you're superior.

1063
01:07:29,171 --> 01:07:30,797
Who the hell are you to...

1064
01:07:31,006 --> 01:07:32,007
You don't even know me.

1065
01:07:32,090 --> 01:07:33,091
Am I wrong?

1066
01:07:35,594 --> 01:07:36,845
Takes one to know one.

1067
01:07:38,931 --> 01:07:39,932
True.

1068
01:07:44,603 --> 01:07:45,979
So, what makes you so superior?

1069
01:07:51,068 --> 01:07:52,236
I can read minds.

1070
01:07:53,070 --> 01:07:54,154
Oh, really?

1071
01:07:54,863 --> 01:07:56,323
Yeah, absolutely.

1072
01:07:56,907 --> 01:07:58,575
All right, what am I thinking right now?

1073
01:08:05,999 --> 01:08:07,084
You're thinking,

1074
01:08:07,876 --> 01:08:10,170
"Charm class isn't helping this situation."

1075
01:08:11,380 --> 01:08:13,131
Wow. Amazing.

1076
01:08:14,549 --> 01:08:15,676
You're thinking,

1077
01:08:17,678 --> 01:08:20,681
"Why does everyone always get
what they want and I get nothing?

1078
01:08:21,014 --> 01:08:22,724
"That I'm tired of being tough all the time."

1079
01:08:24,935 --> 01:08:26,019
Everyone thinks that.

1080
01:08:27,771 --> 01:08:29,064
You pretend like love

1081
01:08:30,023 --> 01:08:31,942
doesn't matter to you, when the truth is

1082
01:08:32,025 --> 01:08:33,860
it's all you ever think about.

1083
01:08:34,069 --> 01:08:35,070
That's not true.

1084
01:08:37,531 --> 01:08:38,532
Okay.

1085
01:08:38,949 --> 01:08:40,117
What, you don't believe me?

1086
01:08:40,367 --> 01:08:41,743
You've known me for a whole hour.

1087
01:08:42,828 --> 01:08:44,204
You've never been in love.

1088
01:08:44,913 --> 01:08:46,081
That's none of your business.

1089
01:08:46,707 --> 01:08:48,041
That's not an answer.

1090
01:08:48,125 --> 01:08:49,626
What makes you think you deserve one?

1091
01:08:51,753 --> 01:08:52,754
You're right.

1092
01:08:53,547 --> 01:08:54,923
I'm sorry for being so direct.

1093
01:09:00,721 --> 01:09:02,889
You said that I'm not how you imagined.

1094
01:09:03,140 --> 01:09:04,224
Have we met before?

1095
01:09:04,808 --> 01:09:05,892
No, I...

1096
01:09:07,227 --> 01:09:08,603
I don't know why I said that.

1097
01:09:08,687 --> 01:09:09,896
Because I feel like we have.

1098
01:09:11,982 --> 01:09:13,900
Things haven't been easy for you, have they?

1099
01:09:16,737 --> 01:09:17,988
Everyone's got problems.

1100
01:09:18,280 --> 01:09:19,281
<i>Yeah.</i>

1101
01:09:20,407 --> 01:09:22,075
<i>We all trip up along the way.</i>

1102
01:09:23,327 --> 01:09:24,619
But you and I,

1103
01:09:26,621 --> 01:09:28,248
perhaps over the same things.

1104
01:09:30,250 --> 01:09:32,210
<i>Mr. Robertson, it's good to see you again.</i>

1105
01:09:32,794 --> 01:09:33,879
It's been a while.

1106
01:09:35,088 --> 01:09:36,089
Yes.

1107
01:09:38,759 --> 01:09:40,385
From your perspective, I suppose it has.

1108
01:09:41,094 --> 01:09:42,763
I didn't think you jumped anymore.

1109
01:09:43,221 --> 01:09:44,806
Only on special occasions.

1110
01:09:45,932 --> 01:09:48,977
I have a piece of the Fizzle Bomber's timer.

1111
01:09:56,818 --> 01:09:59,321
You made an illegal jump.
That's a serious offense.

1112
01:09:59,863 --> 01:10:01,239
It doesn't matter anymore.

1113
01:10:02,240 --> 01:10:03,700
I had to try again.

1114
01:10:03,909 --> 01:10:05,077
And did you apprehend him?

1115
01:10:05,577 --> 01:10:06,578
No.

1116
01:10:08,288 --> 01:10:11,333
The fragments of matter you leave behind
after each jump

1117
01:10:11,416 --> 01:10:13,168
we can only repair so much.

1118
01:10:13,251 --> 01:10:15,796
The onset of psychosis, dementia.

1119
01:10:15,879 --> 01:10:17,005
It can be serious.

1120
01:10:17,839 --> 01:10:18,840
I'm fine.

1121
01:10:19,132 --> 01:10:20,842
How many illegal jumps have you made?

1122
01:10:21,093 --> 01:10:22,094
Just one.

1123
01:10:22,928 --> 01:10:23,929
I'll accept the punishment.

1124
01:10:29,101 --> 01:10:33,438
The parameters set by the Bureau
are strict for a reason.

1125
01:10:33,814 --> 01:10:35,816
They exist for our protection.

1126
01:10:37,818 --> 01:10:38,902
However,

1127
01:10:40,070 --> 01:10:42,989
I've always thought we could accomplish
so much more

1128
01:10:43,073 --> 01:10:46,451
without the constant bureaucratic control
of the board.

1129
01:10:50,163 --> 01:10:51,915
An Agent operating from the outside.

1130
01:10:55,001 --> 01:10:57,754
<i>She'll endure so much pain
because of what I do.</i>

1131
01:10:58,463 --> 01:11:00,006
That's the way it has to be.

1132
01:11:01,007 --> 01:11:02,342
That's the way it's always been.

1133
01:11:03,718 --> 01:11:05,846
You should understand that
better than anyone.

1134
01:11:08,223 --> 01:11:10,976
The snake that eats its own tail,
forever and ever.

1135
01:11:11,977 --> 01:11:14,938
You are here to create history
and influence what is to come.

1136
01:11:15,272 --> 01:11:16,940
I don't think I can do it.

1137
01:11:18,275 --> 01:11:19,276
Understand

1138
01:11:19,359 --> 01:11:20,777
you are more than an Agent.

1139
01:11:20,861 --> 01:11:21,820
You're a gift

1140
01:11:21,903 --> 01:11:23,321
given to the world through a

1141
01:11:23,738 --> 01:11:25,782
Predestination Paradox.

1142
01:11:25,949 --> 01:11:27,284
You're the only one

1143
01:11:27,367 --> 01:11:29,911
free from history, ancestry.

1144
01:11:33,790 --> 01:11:34,958
The rooster.

1145
01:11:36,751 --> 01:11:38,253
But you must complete your mission.

1146
01:11:38,336 --> 01:11:40,005
You must lay the seeds for the future.

1147
01:11:40,881 --> 01:11:42,007
We're counting on you.

1148
01:11:45,051 --> 01:11:48,472
And what happens when that day comes,
when I have no knowledge of my future?

1149
01:11:52,934 --> 01:11:54,019
Well, then, like everyone else

1150
01:11:54,102 --> 01:11:56,146
you're just going to have to take it
one day at a time.

1151
01:12:38,271 --> 01:12:42,359
You have a long journey ahead of you.

1152
01:12:51,952 --> 01:12:54,996
<i>They say that the journey
of a thousand miles</i>

1153
01:12:55,580 --> 01:13:00,126
starts right at your feet.

1154
01:13:02,128 --> 01:13:04,005
And my feet sure could use a rest.

1155
01:13:16,601 --> 01:13:19,229
All right, just going to cover up your eyes

1156
01:13:19,604 --> 01:13:22,274
just to be safe, okay?

1157
01:13:24,359 --> 01:13:27,153
<i>Jumping back almost 20 years can be rough.</i>

1158
01:13:27,404 --> 01:13:28,572
<i>Hold the baby tight.</i>

1159
01:13:28,655 --> 01:13:29,656
You ready?

1160
01:13:29,739 --> 01:13:32,284
<i>And remember, deep breaths.</i>

1161
01:13:44,879 --> 01:13:49,342
<i>Preparation is the key to successful,
inconspicuous time travel.</i>

1162
01:13:52,429 --> 01:13:55,348
<i>Luck is the residue of design.</i>

1163
01:13:56,975 --> 01:13:59,352
<i>Earlier, I had registered as Gregory Johnson,</i>

1164
01:13:59,519 --> 01:14:00,520
<i>Warren, Ohio.</i>

1165
01:14:01,354 --> 01:14:02,480
<i>Keep it simple.</i>

1166
01:14:02,981 --> 01:14:04,024
<i>Blend in.</i>

1167
01:14:17,120 --> 01:14:18,538
Safe journey, Jane.

1168
01:14:19,539 --> 01:14:21,207
Stay strong, John.

1169
01:14:21,625 --> 01:14:23,376
You have a bright future ahead.

1170
01:14:45,523 --> 01:14:47,067
City of Cleveland Orphanage.

1171
01:15:39,119 --> 01:15:40,245
Stay here.

1172
01:15:41,121 --> 01:15:42,122
Where are you going?

1173
01:15:42,956 --> 01:15:43,957
Don't worry.

1174
01:15:44,833 --> 01:15:45,834
I'll be right back.

1175
01:16:13,820 --> 01:16:15,029
You sick fuck.

1176
01:16:15,113 --> 01:16:16,072
You tricked me.

1177
01:16:16,156 --> 01:16:17,657
The choice was yours.

1178
01:16:17,741 --> 01:16:18,783
What choice?

1179
01:16:21,828 --> 01:16:22,871
I'm not going to leave her.

1180
01:16:22,954 --> 01:16:24,330
That's the way that it is.

1181
01:16:24,664 --> 01:16:26,082
It's the way it always has been.

1182
01:16:26,332 --> 01:16:28,293
I'm sorry if you feel deceived.

1183
01:16:29,252 --> 01:16:32,338
But it's a mistake to think that we can
change certain events.

1184
01:16:32,630 --> 01:16:35,008
Just like you said, some things
are inevitable.

1185
01:16:36,593 --> 01:16:38,178
- But I love her.
- I know.

1186
01:16:38,803 --> 01:16:39,804
I know that.

1187
01:16:40,722 --> 01:16:42,015
And now that you've found her

1188
01:16:43,433 --> 01:16:44,642
you know who she is.

1189
01:16:45,143 --> 01:16:47,187
And you understand who you are.

1190
01:16:49,105 --> 01:16:51,649
And now maybe you're ready
to understand who I am.

1191
01:16:59,073 --> 01:17:01,451
Now, listen to me. Listen to me.

1192
01:17:01,868 --> 01:17:03,703
The shock will wear off

1193
01:17:03,787 --> 01:17:06,623
but you can take comfort in knowing
that these events

1194
01:17:06,706 --> 01:17:08,875
are happening in the correct order.

1195
01:17:09,209 --> 01:17:12,170
The path you're on will take you
to your destination.

1196
01:17:14,047 --> 01:17:15,006
Where is that?

1197
01:17:15,089 --> 01:17:17,592
You let me take you to Robertson
and he'll show you everything.

1198
01:17:22,263 --> 01:17:23,723
I don't want to leave her.

1199
01:17:30,021 --> 01:17:31,022
You're not.

1200
01:17:34,651 --> 01:17:36,194
I never wanted to hurt her.

1201
01:17:36,569 --> 01:17:37,570
I know.

1202
01:17:38,363 --> 01:17:39,906
And now she knows too.

1203
01:17:46,663 --> 01:17:47,664
John.

1204
01:17:47,914 --> 01:17:50,250
Listen to me, all right? You're home.

1205
01:17:50,416 --> 01:17:51,793
Your troubles are over.

1206
01:17:51,960 --> 01:17:54,254
You're going to save millions of lives.

1207
01:17:54,712 --> 01:17:58,466
You're about to embark on the most
important job a man has ever had.

1208
01:17:58,925 --> 01:18:01,344
And you're going to do great. I know.

1209
01:18:03,429 --> 01:18:05,849
All right, he's forward jumped 22 years.

1210
01:18:05,932 --> 01:18:07,141
He's not used to this kind of distance.

1211
01:18:10,687 --> 01:18:12,272
John had to want this.

1212
01:18:12,814 --> 01:18:14,190
His life had to be fouled up.

1213
01:18:14,274 --> 01:18:16,693
He had to have nothing in order
to achieve so much.

1214
01:18:17,944 --> 01:18:20,864
A hundred horrible crimes
didn't go as planned, because of him.

1215
01:18:20,947 --> 01:18:22,448
Because of the work you've done.

1216
01:18:23,283 --> 01:18:25,368
But the Fizzle Bomber's still out there.

1217
01:18:26,953 --> 01:18:27,954
I failed.

1218
01:18:28,288 --> 01:18:29,914
He made you a better Agent.

1219
01:18:29,998 --> 01:18:31,082
We've all learned things from him.

1220
01:18:31,165 --> 01:18:32,375
He's made us better at our jobs.

1221
01:18:34,043 --> 01:18:36,129
This organization wouldn't have grown

1222
01:18:36,212 --> 01:18:37,881
if it wasn't for the Fizzle Bomber.

1223
01:18:39,299 --> 01:18:41,050
You sound as if you admire him.

1224
01:18:41,342 --> 01:18:42,385
He's a terrorist.

1225
01:18:42,468 --> 01:18:43,970
Nothing's that simple.

1226
01:18:44,888 --> 01:18:46,014
I wish that it were.

1227
01:18:50,685 --> 01:18:51,686
What's this?

1228
01:18:53,730 --> 01:18:54,772
It's the timer.

1229
01:18:55,565 --> 01:18:56,691
Got some new leads.

1230
01:19:00,320 --> 01:19:02,155
When you reach your final destination

1231
01:19:02,238 --> 01:19:04,115
your Field Kit will decommission...

1232
01:19:06,326 --> 01:19:07,952
As per regulation.

1233
01:19:09,287 --> 01:19:11,456
You sure you want to retire to New York

1234
01:19:12,040 --> 01:19:13,541
so close to the date of the blast?

1235
01:19:15,043 --> 01:19:16,044
Yes, sir.

1236
01:19:19,756 --> 01:19:21,090
You take care of yourself.

1237
01:19:23,176 --> 01:19:24,177
Yes, sir.

1238
01:19:47,825 --> 01:19:50,536
<i>I'm my own grandpa</i>

1239
01:19:51,955 --> 01:19:54,040
<i>I'm my own grandpa</i>

1240
01:19:54,123 --> 01:19:55,792
Jesus H. Christ, Conner!

1241
01:19:56,167 --> 01:19:58,002
Here, look, I'll refund your goddamn money.

1242
01:19:58,670 --> 01:20:00,880
I don't want a refund. Just let me play
the damn song!

1243
01:20:01,214 --> 01:20:03,216
Yeah, come on, Jerry. Let him play
the damn song.

1244
01:20:03,466 --> 01:20:04,550
And by the way, I quit.

1245
01:20:46,175 --> 01:20:47,468
So, this is it.

1246
01:20:48,678 --> 01:20:49,679
Home.

1247
01:21:31,971 --> 01:21:33,514
<i>The order finally came through today.</i>

1248
01:21:34,932 --> 01:21:36,350
<i>I guess it was inevitable.</i>

1249
01:21:37,894 --> 01:21:40,605
<i>By the time you listen to this seven years
will have passed.</i>

1250
01:21:42,315 --> 01:21:45,985
<i>Our first mission
is just as important as our last.</i>

1251
01:21:46,402 --> 01:21:49,989
<i>Each one getting us closer
to our final destination.</i>

1252
01:21:50,656 --> 01:21:52,450
<i>See, you'll find out that time</i>

1253
01:21:52,700 --> 01:21:54,911
<i>has a very different meaning
to people like us.</i>

1254
01:21:56,954 --> 01:21:59,916
<i>Time catches up with us all</i>

1255
01:22:00,500 --> 01:22:02,293
<i>even those in our line of work.</i>

1256
01:22:03,127 --> 01:22:05,004
<i>I guess you could say we're gifted.</i>

1257
01:22:06,047 --> 01:22:09,175
<i>God, Jesus, that sounds arrogant
saying it out loud.</i>

1258
01:22:10,218 --> 01:22:12,512
<i>All right, I'll put it a better way.</i>

1259
01:22:13,221 --> 01:22:14,430
<i>I guess you could say</i>

1260
01:22:15,223 --> 01:22:17,016
<i>we were born into this job.</i>

1261
01:22:23,397 --> 01:22:25,358
You don't see a lot of guys
using these anymore.

1262
01:22:25,441 --> 01:22:27,527
- Is that okay?
- Yeah.

1263
01:22:28,194 --> 01:22:29,195
It's just that...

1264
01:22:29,278 --> 01:22:31,531
I get kind of sentimental about the past.

1265
01:22:32,573 --> 01:22:33,574
That's cool.

1266
01:22:35,701 --> 01:22:36,702
Me too.

1267
01:22:37,286 --> 01:22:38,287
I see.

1268
01:22:42,166 --> 01:22:43,167
<i>So, you're a writer?</i>

1269
01:22:43,501 --> 01:22:45,545
<i>I used to be, I guess.</i>

1270
01:22:45,962 --> 01:22:47,505
<i>And you're thinking of taking it up again?</i>

1271
01:22:48,714 --> 01:22:50,091
I was thinking about it.

1272
01:22:50,633 --> 01:22:52,301
- Right on.
- Yeah.

1273
01:22:52,385 --> 01:22:53,427
What kind of things do you write?

1274
01:22:54,053 --> 01:22:56,389
Oh, just confession stories.

1275
01:22:57,390 --> 01:23:00,143
<i>What, kind of like those
scorned women stories?</i>

1276
01:23:00,726 --> 01:23:04,021
You know, passion, heartbreak, jealousy.

1277
01:23:04,313 --> 01:23:06,649
No, not kinda like, exactly like.

1278
01:23:07,275 --> 01:23:09,235
- Seriously?
- Yeah, seriously.

1279
01:23:10,319 --> 01:23:12,655
<i>You don't look like the type of guy
that'd be into that.</i>

1280
01:23:15,158 --> 01:23:17,076
What do I look like I would be into?

1281
01:23:20,163 --> 01:23:21,247
That's a big question.

1282
01:23:21,998 --> 01:23:25,168
<i>Well, you're interested in this
gorgeous '40 Royal Portable.</i>

1283
01:23:25,251 --> 01:23:26,252
<i>I am.</i>

1284
01:23:26,586 --> 01:23:29,922
Tool of choice for Hemingway,
Kerouac, Fleming.

1285
01:23:30,298 --> 01:23:33,092
And taking into account I've known you
for a whole 30 seconds...

1286
01:23:33,426 --> 01:23:36,012
<i>I'm thinking you're into adventure.</i>

1287
01:23:36,470 --> 01:23:37,513
<i>Suspense.</i>

1288
01:23:37,597 --> 01:23:39,140
<i>Maybe a touch of romance.</i>

1289
01:23:39,348 --> 01:23:43,060
And definitely a big splash of murder.

1290
01:23:43,603 --> 01:23:46,147
- That's stupid, right?
- No, it's not.

1291
01:23:46,272 --> 01:23:48,941
It's never too late to be who
you might have been.

1292
01:24:12,089 --> 01:24:13,633
<i>It's not just the physical injuries.</i>

1293
01:24:14,467 --> 01:24:16,093
<i>You've logged more field hours</i>

1294
01:24:16,177 --> 01:24:18,679
than any of the other Agents
I've been assigned to.

1295
01:24:20,181 --> 01:24:21,641
<i>The risks are real.</i>

1296
01:24:27,230 --> 01:24:29,690
<i>The fragments of matter
you leave behind after each jump</i>

1297
01:24:29,774 --> 01:24:31,651
<i>we can only repair so much.</i>

1298
01:24:31,734 --> 01:24:33,694
The onset of psychosis, dementia.

1299
01:24:33,778 --> 01:24:35,196
That can be serious.

1300
01:24:35,279 --> 01:24:36,280
I'm fine.

1301
01:24:39,283 --> 01:24:41,285
<i>Time travel can be disorienting.</i>

1302
01:24:42,453 --> 01:24:43,996
<i>Don't ever exceed the jump limit.</i>

1303
01:24:44,580 --> 01:24:46,165
It can be problematic.

1304
01:24:49,669 --> 01:24:52,213
<i>The snake that eats its own tail</i>

1305
01:24:52,672 --> 01:24:54,340
<i>forever and ever.</i>

1306
01:24:55,424 --> 01:24:57,260
<i>I know where I come from.</i>

1307
01:24:58,261 --> 01:25:00,513
<i>But where do all you zombies come from?</i>

1308
01:25:26,706 --> 01:25:27,790
Oh, my God.

1309
01:25:30,876 --> 01:25:32,169
You look good.

1310
01:25:35,589 --> 01:25:36,590
I missed you.

1311
01:25:38,551 --> 01:25:39,802
You're the Fizzle Bomber?

1312
01:25:42,388 --> 01:25:45,641
We always hated that name, remember?

1313
01:25:47,393 --> 01:25:48,561
You're a murderer.

1314
01:25:49,228 --> 01:25:53,149
No, no, no. See, I've saved lives,
more than I ever could have

1315
01:25:53,232 --> 01:25:54,692
from inside the bureau.

1316
01:25:54,900 --> 01:25:56,736
No, you kill innocent people.

1317
01:25:57,194 --> 01:25:58,612
Innocent people.

1318
01:25:58,696 --> 01:25:59,697
No, no, no.

1319
01:25:59,780 --> 01:26:02,658
I have clippings from the future.

1320
01:26:02,825 --> 01:26:05,661
Clippings from futures that never happened

1321
01:26:05,745 --> 01:26:07,663
because I prevented them.

1322
01:26:08,831 --> 01:26:12,209
More tragedies prevented, lives saved.

1323
01:26:12,335 --> 01:26:13,336
You see this?

1324
01:26:13,419 --> 01:26:15,296
- Saved?
- Yeah, yeah. Look.

1325
01:26:15,379 --> 01:26:18,466
Look. 1974, Chicago chemical spill.

1326
01:26:18,591 --> 01:26:20,968
That driver never made it to work
in the morning.

1327
01:26:21,427 --> 01:26:25,222
Now, 324 lives saved.

1328
01:26:25,348 --> 01:26:27,475
Look, look. What's next? What's next?

1329
01:26:27,933 --> 01:26:33,606
Right, well we have... We have 1991,
April 3rd, Hamburg, Germany.

1330
01:26:33,689 --> 01:26:37,318
1,861 lives saved.

1331
01:26:37,943 --> 01:26:41,739
The Hardshaw Weapons Factory Heist, 1968.

1332
01:26:41,822 --> 01:26:44,825
You know, the terrorists never came
in the building because I blew it the fuck up.

1333
01:26:45,868 --> 01:26:48,788
3,027 lives I saved.

1334
01:26:49,580 --> 01:26:52,208
Do you keep count of all the civilians
you killed as well?

1335
01:26:52,625 --> 01:26:56,295
Your next attack will kill 10,000 more.

1336
01:26:58,923 --> 01:27:00,758
You're disappointed in me, right?

1337
01:27:00,841 --> 01:27:03,219
I remember that, I do.

1338
01:27:03,302 --> 01:27:04,970
But when the dust settles

1339
01:27:06,680 --> 01:27:09,725
I think you'll see that we did the right thing.

1340
01:27:10,434 --> 01:27:12,269
I will never become you.

1341
01:27:12,645 --> 01:27:14,772
No, I'm curious.

1342
01:27:15,439 --> 01:27:16,816
Did you report

1343
01:27:17,233 --> 01:27:20,319
that your decommissioned Field Kit
didn't decommission?

1344
01:27:21,821 --> 01:27:22,822
Right?

1345
01:27:23,447 --> 01:27:25,658
Some people say that it's fate.

1346
01:27:26,659 --> 01:27:27,952
But you and I,

1347
01:27:28,494 --> 01:27:29,495
we know

1348
01:27:29,745 --> 01:27:31,455
some things are predestined.

1349
01:27:31,872 --> 01:27:34,583
I made you who you are.
You made me who I am.

1350
01:27:34,667 --> 01:27:35,918
It's a paradox, right?

1351
01:27:36,001 --> 01:27:37,837
But it can't be paradoctored.

1352
01:27:39,463 --> 01:27:40,506
Right?

1353
01:27:40,673 --> 01:27:43,676
I had so much fun at preempting you, I did.

1354
01:27:43,843 --> 01:27:46,345
And now you're free and you found me

1355
01:27:46,846 --> 01:27:48,806
and we can be together.

1356
01:27:49,348 --> 01:27:50,641
I'll never become you.

1357
01:27:50,724 --> 01:27:51,725
Don't say that.

1358
01:27:51,892 --> 01:27:52,893
Don't say that.

1359
01:27:53,602 --> 01:27:54,603
We're just puppets.

1360
01:27:55,938 --> 01:27:57,481
We are Robertson.

1361
01:27:57,565 --> 01:27:58,691
He set the whole thing up.

1362
01:27:59,984 --> 01:28:01,026
He played us for fools.

1363
01:28:01,277 --> 01:28:02,695
He's laying out the dominoes.

1364
01:28:02,778 --> 01:28:04,447
You know, we're just watching it fall.

1365
01:28:04,530 --> 01:28:06,824
I will never become you

1366
01:28:06,907 --> 01:28:09,785
and I will not let you kill those people.

1367
01:28:09,869 --> 01:28:10,870
Wait, wait, wait.

1368
01:28:11,036 --> 01:28:13,372
What, you're gonna live a regular life

1369
01:28:13,456 --> 01:28:16,375
with that bitch, Alice, from the antique store?

1370
01:28:17,001 --> 01:28:18,669
She has a stupid cat,

1371
01:28:18,752 --> 01:28:21,964
she has a disgusting birthmark
on her left hip.

1372
01:28:22,047 --> 01:28:23,716
She's a lousy fucking cook.

1373
01:28:23,799 --> 01:28:24,800
Okay, trust me.

1374
01:28:24,884 --> 01:28:26,635
She can't handle our secrets.

1375
01:28:26,719 --> 01:28:28,971
She can't, trust me. She's not right for us.

1376
01:28:29,430 --> 01:28:33,476
You have no idea what is right for me.

1377
01:28:33,559 --> 01:28:36,812
Okay, okay, okay, all we have is each other.

1378
01:28:36,896 --> 01:28:39,565
It is all we've ever had.

1379
01:28:40,316 --> 01:28:41,775
Now if you shoot me

1380
01:28:42,610 --> 01:28:43,694
you'll become me.

1381
01:28:44,612 --> 01:28:45,738
You get it?

1382
01:28:45,821 --> 01:28:47,406
That's how it happens.

1383
01:28:47,615 --> 01:28:49,492
If you want to break the chain

1384
01:28:49,825 --> 01:28:51,368
you have to not kill me

1385
01:28:52,578 --> 01:28:56,582
but try to love me, again.

1386
01:28:58,792 --> 01:29:00,419
What if I put him in front of you,

1387
01:29:01,420 --> 01:29:03,255
the man who ruined your life...

1388
01:29:05,841 --> 01:29:06,842
Forget all that.

1389
01:29:06,926 --> 01:29:08,761
We can have a future together.

1390
01:29:09,428 --> 01:29:10,429
Would you kill him

1391
01:29:10,930 --> 01:29:12,389
to save thousands?

1392
01:29:12,473 --> 01:29:14,058
You wanna know what
we're gonna do tomorrow?

1393
01:29:16,602 --> 01:29:17,603
No.

1394
01:29:40,042 --> 01:29:41,043
<i>Here you are</i>

1395
01:29:41,961 --> 01:29:43,879
<i>at the beginning of your new life.</i>

1396
01:29:45,464 --> 01:29:47,091
<i>It can be overwhelming</i>

1397
01:29:47,591 --> 01:29:49,718
<i>knowing the future you're about to create.</i>

1398
01:29:50,803 --> 01:29:53,055
<i>Knowing the purpose of that life.</i>

1399
01:29:55,391 --> 01:29:56,684
You know who she is.

1400
01:29:58,060 --> 01:30:00,396
And you understand who you are.

1401
01:30:01,146 --> 01:30:03,857
And now maybe you're ready
to understand who I am.

1402
01:30:06,735 --> 01:30:09,738
You see I love her, too.

1403
01:30:49,445 --> 01:30:51,739
<i>You'll have to make tough choices.</i>

1404
01:30:53,157 --> 01:30:54,908
<i>You'll influence the past.</i>

1405
01:30:56,869 --> 01:30:58,537
<i>Can we change our futures?</i>

1406
01:30:59,663 --> 01:31:00,664
<i>I don't know.</i>

1407
01:31:02,583 --> 01:31:04,585
<i>The only thing that I know for sure</i>

1408
01:31:05,711 --> 01:31:08,714
<i>is that you are the best thing
that's ever happened to me.</i>

1409
01:31:12,468 --> 01:31:13,886
<i>I miss you dreadfully.</i>

